Owner findings on 0.24.45.0:
- A brief VPN route interruption leaves the recovery message visible for roughly 20–30 seconds although the current music source is held and playback continues.
- The compact header word “Связь” changes baseline/vertical position and color during fast recovery transitions.
- On Next, the previous title disappears; a transient “Проверяем версию песни CELIKOM…” line and/or technical Track ID can flash before the new title arrives.

Diagnostic evidence:
- The supplied W54 capture contains at least 100 ACTIVE_ENTITLEMENT_ROUTE_CHANGED records, 27 ACTIVE_ENTITLEMENT_TIMEOUT records, 33 ACTIVE_ENTITLEMENT_NETWORK_ERROR records, 37 ACTIVE_ENTITLEMENT_NETWORK_SUSPENDED records and 30 NATIVE_ROUTE_RECOVERY_SOURCE_HELD records.
- The current track remains source-held through route recovery. This is evidence of continuity handling, not independent proof of audible decoder output.
- NativeDecoderUrlPropertyObserved=false and ReplacementAudibleProof=NOT_AVAILABLE_FROM_NETWORK_OR_MAPPING. Do NOT weaken the exact current-decoder proof gate or paint a mapping/no-kUrl hold green.

W164 changes:
- Coalesce delayed Windows VPN adapter notifications into an 8-second native-hold burst; keep the last route event as the owner of the recheck.
- Wait for a 3-second quiet period before the final entitlement recheck. The immediate route-recovery request has a 5-second deadline and an 8-second fast-route window. Clear the route hint after a fresh authenticated server response so ordinary polling returns to its normal 15-second cadence.
- No offline entitlement, cached authorization bypass or server authority change. A real server denial/network failure remains fail-closed.
- Keep the compact header label “Связь” fixed-size and vertically centered. Its color follows a fresh native-host heartbeat; a pending server-route recheck alone does not mark a still-live host disconnected. Detailed recovery information remains in the status row.
- During a genuine track-ID handoff, retain the previous visible title/artist for at most 2.5 seconds while the new metadata arrives. Do not expose raw Track ID placeholders. Hide the transient “Проверяем версию песни CELIKOM…” copy while the per-track presence request is pending; show only a returned availability result.
- Exact decoder-source proof remains unchanged. No W23 native host/renderer, audio engine, Yandex files, Android, browser extension, backend, entitlement authority or updater architecture changes.

